DUPLICATE of cave-24dps. Fixed on main by PR #4245 (b3179c0d90); my PR #4246 closed unmerged.

Another session diagnosed the same bug independently and landed first. Their fix has the same shape as mine — lexical comparison first, canonicalised comparison only when that fails — and is strictly more complete:
- isInsideAllowedRoots is EXPORTED, so it is directly testable rather than module-private;
- canonicalisation is memoised instead of realpath per root;
- it fixes a SECOND site I missed, the copyDynamicPackage containment check (~lines 352-359), where projectRoot/node_modules were compared unresolved for the same reason;
- ~50 lines of added tests.

Verified: scripts/sidecar-runtime-closure.test.mjs exits 0 on macOS against current main.

The diagnosis in this bead stands and was correct — realpath'd target compared against unresolved roots, not macOS-specific, reproduces for any checkout reached through a symlinked component. Only the fix was redundant.

THE REAL LESSON IS PROCESS, not the bug. Two sessions found the same defect and neither knew about the other; cave-24dps already existed when I filed cave-awj6q and opened #4246. This is exactly what docs/multi-session-coordination.md describes, and my own memory note says to search open PRs before building. I searched neither. Before starting work on a symptom, check open PRs and recently-created beads for it — the cost here was a full implement/review/CI cycle that had to be thrown away.

Related: cave-24dps, #4245 (the landed fix), #4246 (closed).
